===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|wevel}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wifel||[[beetle#Noun|beetle]]}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*wibil}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*wibilaz}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*webʰel-}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*webʰ-|*(h₁)webʰ-|to [[wave#Verb|wave]], to [[weave#Verb|weave]]}}, said to be from the woven appearance of a weevil’s [[larval]] [[case#Noun|case]],<ref>{{R:OED Online|entry=weevil|code=226840|part of speech=n|date=1926}}</ref> + {{m|ine-pro|*-el-|*-el-, *-l̥-|pos=diminutive or attributive suffix}}; ''see also'' {{l|en|wave}} and {{l|en|weave}}.

Compare {{cog|osx|*wivil|t=beetle}}; {{cog|gml|wevel}}; {{cog|goh|wibil}}, {{m|goh|wipil}} (modern {{cog|de|Wiebel||beetle; [[chafer]]}}); {{cog|lt|vãbalas||beetle; weevil}}; {{cog|non|vifill}}, as in {{m|non|tordyfill||[[dung beetle]], [[scarab]]}} (whence {{cog|nl|tortwevel}}; {{cog|is|tordýfill}}, {{cog|no|tordivel}}, {{cog|ang|tordwifel}}, {{cog|sv|tordyvel}}); [[Appendix:Glossary#dialectal|dialectal]] {{cog|ru|ве́блица||[[intestinal]] [[worm#Noun|worm]]}}.

