* {{rhymes|en|iːvəl|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|wee|vil}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of many tens of thousands of species of [[herbivorous]] [[beetle]]s, ranging in size from tiny to large, in the [[superfamily]] {{taxfmt|Curculionoidea|superfamily}}, the most characteristic species having the head projecting in a distinctive [[snout]] with the mouthparts at the tip.
# Any of many tens of thousands of species of herbivorous beetles of various sizes, in the [[family]] {{taxfmt|Curculionidae|family}} within the [[superfamily]] Curculionoidea.
# Any of many similar, but more distantly related, beetles such as the {{vern|biscuit weevil}} ({{taxlink|Stegobium paniceum|species}}).
# {{lb|en|figurative|derogatory}} A [[loathsome]] person.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Jack Lindsay|title=Fires in Smithfield. A Novel of Mary Tudor’s Reign|location=London|publisher=w:The Bodley Head|year=1950|page=201|oclc=560679576|passage=But you accuse other men of villainy with too easy a tongue, you '''weevil'''. I have never wanted you in this matter, and I have said so.}}

